## FSR v2 production-hardening plan

**Source of truth:** implementation in `pw_sdg_ai_ser_repo`. Design and RCA
documents are supporting context only; any mismatch must be resolved in favor
of the deployed code and recorded here.

### Verified starting points

- P1 discovers the input set with Spark, but parses, preprocesses, calls the
	enrichment LLM, and writes results in a driver-side sequential loop.
- P2 claims documents in batches and drains the queue, but v2 does not yet
	expose the v1 P2 embedding/PDF worker controls or implement equivalent
	bounded concurrency in the v2 chunking path.
- v2 has separate P1, P2, P3, and validation workflow files, but the bundle
	configuration and target-specific v2 parameters need a complete dev/qa/stg/
	prod audit.
- P1/P2 run-log writes are currently optional and non-blocking. P1 DQ logging
	covers failed metadata documents; P2 needs equivalent per-document failure
	visibility and run-level operational metrics.
- The parsed-document volume is versioned by parser version, but cache
	overwrite, partial-file, stale-file, permission, and source-file-change
	behavior need explicit guarantees before backfill use.
- Retrieval uses `document_id`, ESN mapping, status, dates, and chunk metadata;
	the retrieval guide does not use metadata `title` for eligibility or VS
	filtering. Removing or renaming it still requires a compatibility check.

